# 50mm Retina World · the ONE FFmpeg the converter runs (owner ruling R-VM-1:
# nothing paid or chargeable). An official static GPL build from BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
# (https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds), release line 9.0, from a MONTH-END
# autobuild: BtbN keeps the last build of each month for TWO YEARS (daily ones
# for 14 days), so this exact file stays downloadable until about 2028-09 — and
# a pin older than a few months is overdue for a security update anyway.
#
# Each file is named by its exact URL and sha256. The sha256 values were checked
# three ways on 2026-10-13: BtbN's published checksums.sha256 for this release,
# the digest GitHub reports for each release asset, and hashing the downloaded
# files. setup.sh / update-ffmpeg.sh refuse any file whose sha256 differs, and
# refuse a pin whose URL is not exactly
#   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/<FFMPEG_RELEASE>/<FFMPEG_ASSET_arch>
#
# Licence: GPL version 3 (the build is configured --enable-gpl --enable-version3;
# its LICENSE.txt is installed beside the binaries). The two commits below are the
# exact source: FFmpeg itself (branch release/9.0 = tag n9.0.2 + 17 commits) and
# BtbN's build scripts at this release's tag. See deploy/README.md, "Licence".
#
# To update: deploy/README.md ("FFmpeg: pinned, and how it is kept up to date").
